# CODEOWNERS - only CATASTROPHIC / IRREVERSIBLE paths need an owner.
# Everything else moves freely (no bottleneck). A mistake on the paths below can't be cleanly undone,
# so they require a code-owner's review before merging into main.
#
# THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE. It is rendered per workspace, never copied, because a code owner must be
# somebody with write access to YOUR repository. Render it with:
#
#   python3 scripts/aios/aios.py governance render --repo-slug <owner>/<repo> \
#     --owner "REPO_OWNER=@your-handle" --owner "PRIMARY_REVIEWER=@their-handle" \
#     --out .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# The rendered file carries an `# aios-codeowners-for:` line naming the repository it belongs to,
# so a workspace generated from a template cannot silently inherit somebody else's owners.
#
#   [REPO_OWNER]        = the founder / repo owner
#   [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]  = whoever approves governance changes (often the same person)
#   [TECHNICAL_REVIEWER]= optional second owner for code/migrations
#
# Naming an owner is necessary but NOT sufficient: GitHub only enforces it when branch protection
# on main has "Require review from Code Owners" turned on. Check both with:
#   python3 scripts/aios/aios.py governance check
#   bash scripts/team/verify-branch-protection.sh

# Irreversible - a mistake here can't be cleanly undone
**/migrations/**            [REPO_OWNER] [TECHNICAL_REVIEWER]
**/*.sql                    [REPO_OWNER] [TECHNICAL_REVIEWER]
.env*                       [REPO_OWNER]
.gitignore                  [REPO_OWNER]

# The review/merge gate itself - weakening this dilutes every other guarantee
/.github/                   [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]

# The brain's constitution + the skill/hook engine (governs every session + agent)
/CLAUDE.md                  [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]
/.claude/skills/            [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]
/.claude/settings.json      [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]
/.claude/hooks/             [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]

# Who may operate this workspace, and which release it runs - the install contract's own gate
/.aios/config.json          [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]
/.aios/roles.json           [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]
/releases/                  [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]
/release/                   [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]

# The founder lane: every path an operator's role may not change (.aios/roles.json paths_denied).
# The boundary check fails an operator's PR here until a founder approves; this makes GitHub
# ask the right person for that approval.
/01_Foundations/offer_economics/  [REPO_OWNER]
/scripts/aios/              [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]
/templates/governance/      [REPO_OWNER] [PRIMARY_REVIEWER]

# Deliberately NOT owner-gated: your normal docs, deliverables, and day-to-day work move freely.
